3:["$","div",null,{"lang":"en","children":[["$","$Le",null,{"lang":"en","items":[{"id":"001","slug":"distribution-is-the-moat","category":"doctrine","term":"Account-Generated Distribution","en":{"title":"What Is AGD Marketing? Account-Generated Distribution Explained","dek":"Everyone can produce. Almost nobody knows how to distribute. Welcome to the other side of the iceberg."}},{"id":"002","slug":"ai-sameness","category":"creative","term":"AI Slop","en":{"title":"AI Content for Social Media: How to Avoid Generic Output","dek":"Perfect faces. Interchangeable scripts. Creativity is not measured in exports per minute."}},{"id":"003","slug":"account-isolation","category":"doctrine","term":"Account Isolation","en":{"title":"Account Isolation in AGD: Build Distinct Social Accounts","dek":"Account Isolation: differentiate the voices before multiplying the profiles."}},{"id":"004","slug":"native-vs-api","category":"lab","term":"Native Posting","en":{"title":"Native Posting vs API Posting on TikTok: What Can You Test?","dek":"“APIs kill reach.” Here is the protocol that claim would need."}},{"id":"005","slug":"agent-first-dry-run","category":"machines","term":"Agentic AGD","en":{"title":"TokPortal MCP Tutorial: Preview an AI Workflow with Dry Run","dek":"A real MCP workflow starts with a readable preview, not a surprise charge."}},{"id":"006","slug":"multi-account-strategy","category":"doctrine","term":"Multi-Account Strategy","en":{"title":"AGD for TikTok 101: Accounts, Content and Your First Tests","dek":"A Multi-Account Strategy distributes a brand’s experiments across differentiated accounts."}},{"id":"007","slug":"content-isolation","category":"doctrine","term":"Content Isolation","en":{"title":"Content Isolation: How to Differentiate a Multi-Account Strategy","dek":"Content Isolation preserves meaningful creative differences between accounts: narrative, angle, format or purpose."}},{"id":"008","slug":"content-saturation","category":"doctrine","term":"Content Saturation","en":{"title":"Social Media Content Saturation: What It Means for AGD","dek":"Content Saturation describes content supply exceeding available attention."}},{"id":"009","slug":"feed-escalation","category":"doctrine","term":"Feed Escalation","en":{"title":"How AGD Changes the Competition for Organic Reach","dek":"Feed Escalation is our editorial term for intensifying formats, output and optimization inside feeds."}},{"id":"010","slug":"attention-war","category":"doctrine","term":"Attention War","en":{"title":"Organic Social Media for SaaS: Competing for Attention","dek":"Attention War is our cultural shorthand for competition over limited attention among content, people and platforms."}},{"id":"011","slug":"agd-not-phone-farm","category":"doctrine","term":"Phone Farming","en":{"title":"AGD vs Phone Farms: Strategy, Accounts and Infrastructure","dek":"Phone Farming describes infrastructure for operating accounts across mobile environments."}},{"id":"012","slug":"agd-without-tokportal","category":"doctrine","term":"AGD & infrastructure","en":{"title":"How to Build an AGD Strategy with Your Existing Tools","dek":"AGD is a strategy framework. TokPortal provides infrastructure that can support execution. A category that only works with one brand mostly looks like a campaign."}},{"id":"013","slug":"ten-principles","category":"doctrine","term":"AGD principles","en":{"title":"AGD Marketing Principles: A Practical Editorial Framework","dek":"AGD principles combine differentiated accounts, creative diversity, contextual execution and measurable learning."}},{"id":"014","slug":"anti-principles","category":"doctrine","term":"AGD anti-principles","en":{"title":"AGD Marketing Mistakes: Volume, Copying and False Promises","dek":"AGD anti-principles challenge clones, volume without diversity, certainty without data and averages without context."}},{"id":"015","slug":"native-account","category":"doctrine","term":"Native Account","en":{"title":"What Is a Native TikTok Account? Context and Limitations","dek":"In the AGD lexicon, a Native Account is created and maintained in the real consumer application environment."}},{"id":"016","slug":"account-persona","category":"creative","term":"Account Persona","en":{"title":"How to Build a Social Media Persona: The Duolingo Example","dek":"An Account Persona is the recurring identity that gives an account a perspective: who speaks, to whom, and why people return.."}},{"id":"017","slug":"hook-slop","category":"creative","term":"Hook Slop","en":{"title":"TikTok Hook Examples: Replace Clickbait with a Clear Payoff","dek":"Hook Slop means intense but interchangeable openings disconnected from the content’s actual value."}},{"id":"018","slug":"faceless-account","category":"creative","term":"Faceless Account","en":{"title":"Faceless TikTok Accounts: Formats, Voice and Content Strategy","dek":"A Faceless Account creates content without relying on its operator’s visible face."}},{"id":"019","slug":"formatted-account","category":"creative","term":"Formatted Account","en":{"title":"TikTok Content Series: Build a Repeatable Format","dek":"A Formatted Account uses a repeatable creative structure an audience can recognize."}},{"id":"020","slug":"chaotic-account","category":"creative","term":"Chaotic Account","en":{"title":"Duolingo’s TikTok Strategy: Character, Chaos and Continuity","dek":"A Chaotic Account allows several formats rather than one rigid template."}},{"id":"021","slug":"ai-persona","category":"creative","term":"AI Persona","en":{"title":"AI Personas for Social Media: Character Design and Disclosure","dek":"An AI Persona substantially uses AI for appearance, voice or production."}},{"id":"022","slug":"persona-agd","category":"creative","term":"Persona AGD","en":{"title":"Persona-Based AGD: Give Each Account a Distinct Voice","dek":"Persona AGD organizes a network around distinct editorial characters rather than generic brand accounts.."}},{"id":"023","slug":"slideshow-agd","category":"creative","term":"Slideshow AGD","en":{"title":"TikTok Slideshow Strategy: Story Structure for AGD","dek":"Slideshow AGD uses accounts publishing native carousels or slideshows."}},{"id":"024","slug":"story-slideshow","category":"creative","term":"Story Slideshow","en":{"title":"How to Structure a TikTok Slideshow as a Story","dek":"A Story Slideshow organizes a sequence around a situation and its resolution."}},{"id":"025","slug":"educational-slideshow","category":"creative","term":"Educational Slideshow","en":{"title":"Educational TikTok Content: Turn a Real Process into a Story","dek":"An educational slideshow communicates usable knowledge during reading."}},{"id":"026","slug":"meme-slideshow","category":"creative","term":"Meme Slideshow","en":{"title":"Brand Memes on TikTok: What Ryanair’s Persona Can Teach You","dek":"A Meme Slideshow builds its sequence around a cultural observation or punchline."}},{"id":"027","slug":"product-discovery","category":"creative","term":"Product Discovery","en":{"title":"TikTok Product Discovery: Lessons from the Ocean Spray Video","dek":"Product discovery content introduces a tool inside an understandable use case."}},{"id":"028","slug":"brainrotization","category":"creative","term":"Brainrotization","en":{"title":"Brainrot Marketing: When Internet Culture Helps a Brand","dek":"Brainrotization is our cultural shorthand for fast, absurd and compressed feed formats."}},{"id":"029","slug":"creative-brief","category":"creative","term":"Creative Brief","en":{"title":"How to Write a TikTok Creative Brief with a Concrete Example","dek":"An AGD creative brief connects audience, promise, format and hypothesis."}},{"id":"030","slug":"hook-payoff","category":"creative","term":"Hook & payoff","en":{"title":"TikTok Hooks and Payoffs: A Zach King Video Breakdown","dek":"The payoff is the narrative or practical answer to the opening promise."}},{"id":"031","slug":"creative-library","category":"creative","term":"Creative Library","en":{"title":"How to Build a TikTok Creative Library from Real Examples","dek":"A creative library organizes concepts, versions, rights and results."}},{"id":"032","slug":"format-fatigue","category":"creative","term":"Format fatigue","en":{"title":"TikTok Content Fatigue: When to Refresh a Recurring Format","dek":"Format fatigue is a hypothesis about weakening response after repetition."}},{"id":"033","slug":"creative-matrix","category":"creative","term":"Creative Matrix","en":{"title":"Creative Testing Matrix: Lessons from LEGO’s Instagram Reel","dek":"A creative matrix crosses variation dimensions: audience, problem, angle and format."}},{"id":"034","slug":"niche-warming","category":"field-notes","term":"Niche Warming","en":{"title":"TikTok Account Warming: Define a Relevant, Testable Routine","dek":"Niche Warming means exploring niche content in the app through searches, viewing and authentic interactions."}},{"id":"035","slug":"native-posting","category":"field-notes","term":"Native Posting","en":{"title":"Native TikTok Posting: Workflow, Features and Quality Checks","dek":"Native Posting means publishing through a platform’s consumer interface."}},{"id":"036","slug":"native-warming","category":"field-notes","term":"Native Warming","en":{"title":"Native Account Warming: Actions, Records and Limits","dek":"Native Warming happens in the real application through ordinary, authentic interactions."}},{"id":"037","slug":"geo-targeted-account","category":"field-notes","term":"Geo-Targeted Account","en":{"title":"US TikTok Accounts: Geography, Setup and Audience Limits","dek":"A Geo-Targeted Account is established and operated in its target market."}},{"id":"038","slug":"geo-posting","category":"field-notes","term":"Geo-Posting","en":{"title":"Geo-Posting for TikTok: Location Context vs Audience Targeting","dek":"Geo-Posting means publishing through an account operated in the target market."}},{"id":"039","slug":"us-launch","category":"field-notes","term":"US launch","en":{"title":"How to Reach US TikTok Audiences from Abroad","dek":"An international launch needs an understandable offer and a locally relevant use case."}},{"id":"040","slug":"localization-not-translation","category":"field-notes","term":"Localization","en":{"title":"TikTok Content Localization: Go Beyond Translation","dek":"Localization adapts meaning, references and uses."}},{"id":"041","slug":"account-brief","category":"field-notes","term":"Account Brief","en":{"title":"Social Media Account Brief: Audience, Voice and Publishing Rules","dek":"An account brief sets its promise, audience, voice and boundaries."}},{"id":"042","slug":"operator-handoff","category":"field-notes","term":"Operator handoff","en":{"title":"Social Publishing Handoffs: What to Give Your Operator","dek":"A handoff transfers an executable task with assets, constraints and success conditions."}},{"id":"043","slug":"publishing-window","category":"field-notes","term":"Publishing window","en":{"title":"TikTok Publishing Schedule: Plan Windows, Not Magic Minutes","dek":"A publishing window defines an acceptable interval for a task."}},{"id":"044","slug":"account-inventory","category":"field-notes","term":"Account inventory","en":{"title":"How to Organize a Multi-Account Social Media Inventory","dek":"An AGD inventory connects each account to its role, market, owner and observed state."}},{"id":"045","slug":"zero-views","category":"field-notes","term":"Stuck at 0 views","en":{"title":"Why Does My TikTok Have Zero Views? A Diagnostic Workflow","dek":"Stuck at 0 views describes low or absent distribution after publication."}},{"id":"046","slug":"shadowban","category":"field-notes","term":"Shadowban","en":{"title":"TikTok Shadowban or Low Reach? How to Investigate","dek":"Shadowban is an informal term for suspected distribution suppression without explicit notice."}},{"id":"047","slug":"distribution-failure","category":"field-notes","term":"Distribution failure","en":{"title":"TikTok Publishing Failures: Separate Upload, Access and Reach","dek":"A distribution failure can involve account access, a feature, removed content, a missing publication or weak reach."}},{"id":"048","slug":"native-not-deceptive","category":"field-notes","term":"Commercial transparency","en":{"title":"Organic Brand Accounts: Native Content and Transparent Identity","dek":"Content can be useful, native and commercial at once."}},{"id":"049","slug":"reddit-agd","category":"field-notes","term":"Reddit AGD","en":{"title":"Reddit Marketing and AGD: Contribute Before You Promote","dek":"Reddit AGD adapts account differentiation to legitimate community participation."}},{"id":"050","slug":"community-distribution","category":"field-notes","term":"Community distribution","en":{"title":"Community Marketing: How Brands Join Existing Conversations","dek":"A community is not merely an acquisition channel."}},{"id":"051","slug":"content-rights","category":"field-notes","term":"Content rights","en":{"title":"Social Media Content Rights: A Publishing Checklist","dek":"A provenance register connects images, sounds and videos to their origins and checked usage conditions."}},{"id":"052","slug":"campaign-retrospective","category":"field-notes","term":"Campaign retrospective","en":{"title":"AGD Campaign Review: Creative, Distribution and Evidence","dek":"An AGD retrospective connects objectives, execution, observations and decisions."}},{"id":"053","slug":"budget-of-learning","category":"field-notes","term":"Learning budget","en":{"title":"How to Budget an AGD Experiment: Costs and Learning Goals","dek":"A learning budget includes production, coordination, execution and analysis."}},{"id":"054","slug":"viral-hit","category":"lab","term":"Viral Hit","en":{"title":"What Counts as a Viral TikTok? Define the Comparison","dek":"A Viral Hit is an unusually high distribution outcome relative to a defined baseline: account, cohort or campaign."}},{"id":"055","slug":"viral-hit-rate","category":"lab","term":"Viral Hit Rate","en":{"title":"TikTok Viral Hit Rate: Define Attempts and Measure Outcomes","dek":"Viral Hit Rate is the proportion of eligible posts exceeding a predefined outlier threshold."}},{"id":"056","slug":"median-vs-mean","category":"lab","term":"Median vs mean","en":{"title":"TikTok Analytics: Average vs Median Views Explained","dek":"The mean adds values and divides by their count."}},{"id":"057","slug":"percentiles","category":"lab","term":"Distribution percentiles","en":{"title":"Social Media Analytics: How to Read Performance Percentiles","dek":"A percentile locates a value in an ordered distribution."}},{"id":"058","slug":"power-law","category":"lab","term":"Distribution concentration","en":{"title":"Why a Few TikTok Posts Can Dominate Your Reach","dek":"Concentration measures the share of outcomes produced by a fraction of posts."}},{"id":"059","slug":"top-ten-accounts","category":"lab","term":"Account concentration","en":{"title":"Multi-Account Analytics: Measure Performance Concentration","dek":"Account concentration shows which assets carry the total outcome."}},{"id":"060","slug":"matched-cohorts","category":"lab","term":"Matched cohorts","en":{"title":"How to Compare TikTok Campaigns with Matched Cohorts","dek":"A matched cohort aligns observations on known characteristics."}},{"id":"061","slug":"posting-time-myth","category":"lab","term":"Posting-time myth","en":{"title":"Best Time to Post on TikTok? Test Timing Without the Myths","dek":"Posting-time effects may depend on audience and context."}},{"id":"062","slug":"posting-frequency","category":"lab","term":"Posting frequency","en":{"title":"How Often Should You Post on TikTok? Design a Useful Test","dek":"A frequency test must separate total volume, per-post performance and production load."}},{"id":"063","slug":"warming-study","category":"lab","term":"Warming protocol","en":{"title":"Does TikTok Account Warming Work? An Experiment Protocol","dek":"A warming protocol compares preparations defined before publishing."}},{"id":"064","slug":"account-age","category":"lab","term":"Account age","en":{"title":"Does TikTok Account Age Affect Reach? What to Compare","dek":"Account age can be associated with history, followers and behavior."}},{"id":"065","slug":"slideshow-vs-video","category":"lab","term":"Slideshow vs video","en":{"title":"TikTok Slideshows vs Videos: How to Compare the Formats","dek":"Comparing slideshow and video requires a comparable promise and audience."}},{"id":"066","slug":"formatted-vs-chaotic","category":"lab","term":"Formatted vs chaotic","en":{"title":"TikTok Content Strategy: Recurring Series vs Spontaneous Posts","dek":"A Formatted versus Chaotic test compares a recurring structure with multiple formats."}},{"id":"067","slug":"creative-diversity-test","category":"lab","term":"Creative diversity","en":{"title":"TikTok Creative Testing: Compare Ideas, Not Just Edits","dek":"A creative-diversity test examines meaningful variation rather than counting files."}},{"id":"068","slug":"native-features-test","category":"lab","term":"Native features","en":{"title":"TikTok Native Features: Test Their Creative Contribution","dek":"A native-feature test separates a feature’s effect from its publishing channel."}},{"id":"069","slug":"zero-view-rate","category":"lab","term":"Zero-view rate","en":{"title":"How to Measure Your TikTok Zero-View Rate","dek":"Zero-view rate depends on observation age, measurement source and eligibility scope."}},{"id":"070","slug":"confidence-intervals","category":"lab","term":"Uncertainty","en":{"title":"Social Media Experiments: Confidence Intervals Explained","dek":"An interval expresses uncertainty under a method’s assumptions."}},{"id":"071","slug":"survivorship-bias","category":"lab","term":"Survivorship bias","en":{"title":"TikTok Case Studies and Survivorship Bias: What Is Missing?","dek":"Survivorship bias appears when analysis retains only still-visible units."}},{"id":"072","slug":"regression-to-mean","category":"lab","term":"Regression to the mean","en":{"title":"Why TikTok Views Drop After a Viral Post","dek":"An extreme outcome can be followed by more ordinary outcomes."}},{"id":"073","slug":"cohort-maturity","category":"lab","term":"Cohort maturity","en":{"title":"Campaign Cohort Analysis: Compare Equally Mature Results","dek":"Day-seven conversion should cover people given seven full days to convert."}},{"id":"074","slug":"attribution","category":"lab","term":"Attribution","en":{"title":"TikTok Marketing Attribution: UTMs, Visits and First Purchases","dek":"Campaign parameters describe an instrumented origin."}},{"id":"075","slug":"views-to-buyers","category":"lab","term":"Views to buyers","en":{"title":"From TikTok Views to Sales: Measure the Customer Journey","dek":"Views measure exposure under the platform’s definition."}},{"id":"076","slug":"experiment-preregistration","category":"lab","term":"Preregistration","en":{"title":"Social Media Experiment Template: Write the Plan First","dek":"Preregistering means recording an experiment’s question, criteria and planned analysis in advance."}},{"id":"077","slug":"stop-rules","category":"lab","term":"Stop rules","en":{"title":"When to Stop an AGD Experiment: Budget and Evidence Rules","dek":"A stop rule specifies when to end, pause or reconsider an experiment."}},{"id":"078","slug":"evidence-ladder","category":"lab","term":"Evidence ladder","en":{"title":"How to Evaluate AGD Claims: Documentation, Examples and Tests","dek":"The AGD evidence ladder separates platform documentation, methodical proprietary data, controlled experiments, repeated observations, hypotheses and folklore."}},{"id":"079","slug":"ai-agd","category":"machines","term":"AI AGD","en":{"title":"AI for AGD Marketing: From Creative Brief to Publishing Workflow","dek":"AI AGD means using AI to plan, produce, analyze or orchestrate AGD."}},{"id":"080","slug":"agentic-agd","category":"machines","term":"Agentic AGD","en":{"title":"Agentic AGD: What an AI Distribution Agent Should Do","dek":"Agentic AGD coordinates recurring decisions across accounts, content, markets and experiments."}},{"id":"081","slug":"human-api","category":"machines","term":"Human API","en":{"title":"TokPortal’s Human API: Briefs, Native Actions and Receipts","dek":"A Human API exposes a software workflow partly executed by people."}},{"id":"082","slug":"mcp-orchestration","category":"machines","term":"MCP orchestration","en":{"title":"TokPortal MCP Workflows: Connect AI to Social Operations","dek":"MCP lets an agent client discover and call tools exposed by a server."}},{"id":"083","slug":"dry-run-contract","category":"machines","term":"Dry-run contract","en":{"title":"What Does a TokPortal Dry Run Do? Preview Scope and Limits","dek":"A dry run validates a request without producing live effects under the service’s contract."}},{"id":"084","slug":"idempotency","category":"machines","term":"Idempotency","en":{"title":"API Retry Safety: Avoid Duplicate Social Publishing Operations","dek":"Idempotency prevents repeated execution of one intent from producing multiple effects when supported by the operation’s contract."}},{"id":"085","slug":"webhooks","category":"machines","term":"Webhooks","en":{"title":"Social Publishing Webhooks: Events, Status and Recovery","dek":"A webhook sends an event to your integration."}},{"id":"086","slug":"agent-budget","category":"machines","term":"Agent budgets","en":{"title":"How to Set a Budget for an AI Marketing Agent","dek":"An agent budget defines authorized operations, limits and renewal conditions."}},{"id":"087","slug":"agent-maturity","category":"machines","term":"AGD maturity model","en":{"title":"AI Marketing Automation: When to Increase Agent Autonomy","dek":"The AGD model distinguishes manual work, AI assistance, approved orchestration, agentic management and broader autonomy."}},{"id":"088","slug":"api-slop","category":"machines","term":"API Slop","en":{"title":"Social Media API Automation: Keep the Editorial Brief Intact","dek":"API Slop criticizes mass delivery of undifferentiated content without attention to accounts or context."}},{"id":"089","slug":"content-routing","category":"machines","term":"Content routing","en":{"title":"Content Routing for Multiple Social Accounts","dek":"Routing connects creative work to an account by audience, persona, market and purpose."}},{"id":"090","slug":"creative-clustering","category":"machines","term":"Creative clustering","en":{"title":"How to Organize Social Creative by Idea and Mechanism","dek":"Creative clustering groups content under chosen criteria."}},{"id":"091","slug":"anomaly-detection","category":"machines","term":"Anomaly detection","en":{"title":"Social Media Monitoring: Build Useful Operational Alerts","dek":"Anomaly detection flags deviation from a defined baseline."}},{"id":"092","slug":"human-review","category":"machines","term":"Human review","en":{"title":"Human Review for AI Content: Approve the Version That Ships","dek":"Useful human review exposes the action, consequences and evidence to check."}},{"id":"093","slug":"source-of-truth","category":"machines","term":"Source of truth","en":{"title":"Marketing Automation Records: Build a Reliable Source of Truth","dek":"A technical source of truth describes an interface’s current capabilities."}},{"id":"094","slug":"seo-agd","category":"machines","term":"SEO AGD","en":{"title":"AGD and SEO: Turn Social Ideas into Searchable Articles","dek":"SEO AGD explores social content and properties appearing in search engines and platform search."}},{"id":"095","slug":"pseo-agd","category":"machines","term":"pSEO AGD","en":{"title":"Programmatic SEO for AGD: Structure Useful, Distinct Pages","dek":"pSEO AGD systematically organizes social content around distinct search intents."}},{"id":"096","slug":"llm-quoting","category":"machines","term":"LLM quoting","en":{"title":"Writing AGD Content That Search and AI Can Cite","dek":"Citable content clearly states a proposition, scope and provenance."}},{"id":"097","slug":"knowledge-graph","category":"machines","term":"AGD content graph","en":{"title":"Internal Linking for AGD Content: Connect Concepts Clearly","dek":"An editorial graph connects parent concepts, neighbors and applications."}},{"id":"098","slug":"multilingual-seo","category":"machines","term":"Multilingual publishing","en":{"title":"Multilingual Content Strategy: When to Expand Your AGD Site","dek":"A multilingual publication gives each version a stable URL and connects matching translations."}},{"id":"099","slug":"structured-editorial","category":"machines","term":"Structured editorial","en":{"title":"AGD Article Schema: Structure Text, Stories and Real Examples","dek":"An editorial schema requires publishing essentials: identity, translations, media, stories, text, sources and links."}},{"id":"100","slug":"agent-audit-log","category":"machines","term":"Agent audit log","en":{"title":"AI Agent Audit Logs: Trace Marketing Actions and Decisions","dek":"An agent log connects intent, tool, result and next decision."}}]}],"$Lf","$L10"]}]
11:T648,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Article","@id":"https://naybu256.github.io/en/read/lab/creative-diversity-test/#article","headline":"TikTok Creative Testing: Compare Ideas, Not Just Edits","description":"A creative-diversity test examines meaningful variation rather than counting files.","inLanguage":"en","datePublished":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","dateModified":"2026-09-09T07:43:10.585Z","image":["https://naybu256.github.io/images/editorial/creative-diversity-test.jpg"],"author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Jet","url":"https://naybu256.github.io/en/about/#jet","image":"https://naybu256.github.io/images/authors/jet.jpg"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"THE ORGANIC CLUB","url":"https://naybu256.github.io"},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://naybu256.github.io/en/read/lab/creative-diversity-test/","articleSection":"The Lab","wordCount":567,"citation":["https://www.tiktok.com/@jack.designs/video/7250198864270052634","https://newsroom.tiktok.com/cleantokawards?lang=en-GB","https://www.tiktok.com/@stevienicks/video/6883220570914278662","https://newsroom.tiktok.com/doggface-gives-the-world-a-smile-with-juice-a-skateboard-and-all-the-vibes?lang=en"]},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"THE ORGANIC CLUB","item":"https://naybu256.github.io/en/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"The Lab","item":"https://naybu256.github.io/en/topics/lab/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"TikTok Creative Testing: Compare Ideas, Not Just Edits","item":"https://naybu256.github.io/en/read/lab/creative-diversity-test/"}]}]}1:["$","main",null,{"id":"main","className":"main-shell","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$11"}}],["$","$L12",null,{"article":{"id":"067","slug":"creative-diversity-test","term":"Creative diversity","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"creative-diversity-test","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["native-features-test","formatted-vs-chaotic","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"TikTok Creative Testing: Compare Ideas, Not Just Edits","dek":"A creative-diversity test examines meaningful variation rather than counting files.","point":"A creative-diversity test examines meaningful variation rather than counting files. It connects concepts with outcomes and their stability.","body":["Label angles, personas and situations before examining performance. Compare similar-volume groups with documented diversity differences. Keep costs visible: more angles may require more design work. Ask whether the difference improves useful learning, not merely outcome dispersion.","A blind review can help: hide results and ask several people to classify creative work using the taxonomy. Disagreements expose vague categories. This does not measure marketing impact, but checks whether the definition of diversity can be applied without already knowing winners. Keep ambiguous cases visible and revise the coding guide before using those categories to explain performance or allocate the next production budget."],"action":["Define a simple creative taxonomy.","Measure outcomes and design effort."],"trap":"A taxonomy invented after reading results can rationalize successes.","quote":"Diversity also lives in what you learn.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Diversity also lives in what you learn.","text":"A creative-diversity test examines meaningful variation rather than counting files.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-diversity-test.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Creative diversity","text":"A creative-diversity test examines meaningful variation rather than counting files. It connects concepts with outcomes and their stability.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-diversity-test.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A taxonomy invented after reading results can rationalize successes.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-diversity-test.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Define a simple creative taxonomy.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-diversity-test.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Measure outcomes and design effort.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-diversity-test.jpg"}]}]},"workshops":[],"schemaVersion":2,"deepDive":{"heading":"Count distinct hypotheses, not exported files","paragraphs":["A folder of thirty edits can contain one idea. Different subtitles, crops and backing tracks may help optimise execution, but they do not necessarily test different reasons for someone to care. Label each creative by the audience problem, claim, proof and narrative device before counting diversity. A price objection, a workflow demonstration and a surprising use case are meaningfully different propositions even when they use the same visual template. This distinction prevents a large production queue from masquerading as a broad exploration of demand.","Choose a manageable set of hypotheses and give each enough execution quality to be a fair attempt. Keep the downstream destination coherent so a successful opening does not lead to an unrelated offer. After publication, review the comments for evidence about interpretation as well as the performance metrics. A low-view post that reveals a serious misunderstanding may improve the next brief. Preserve the labels and failed attempts in the creative library. Otherwise the team repeatedly rediscovers the same idea under new filenames and calls the repetition a learning system.","The sink-cleaning example makes sound part of the stated creative treatment. A useful exploration would compare genuinely different ways of explaining a relevant task, not merely swap the music while keeping every promise identical. One treatment might emphasise the transformation, another the difficult step and another the sensory process. Those are candidate hypotheses about what makes the activity interesting. Give each an original, rights-cleared execution and define the intended outcome before publishing. The presence of a named product in the reference is observable context; sponsorship and commercial effectiveness remain separate questions that the available evidence does not resolve."],"diagram":{"kind":"flow","title":"From variants to real exploration","items":[{"label":"Problem","detail":"Which audience tension does the post address?","value":0},{"label":"Proof","detail":"What makes the claim understandable or credible?","value":0},{"label":"Device","detail":"How does the story deliver that evidence?","value":0}],"caption":"Editorial model: a way to reason about the process, not measured platform results."},"caseLens":"Identify the specific audience promise in this example, then design a different promise rather than merely changing its colours or captions.","caseIds":["jack-sink-asmr","stevie-nicks-afternoon"]},"examples":[{"id":"jack-sink-asmr","platform":"tiktok","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@jack.designs/video/7250198864270052634","creator":"Jack Callaghan","title":"The working sound becomes part of the product scene","description":"Jack Callaghan cleans a sink; his caption explicitly names Cif and presents the post as cleaning ASMR. TikTok’s shortlist describes the sink scrub.","mechanism":"Consider which sounds make the process understandable or satisfying. Product placement is more legible when the audience can connect the product to the action.","limitation":"Establishes an ASMR-labelled demonstration with a named product. Sponsorship, sales and comparative cleaning effectiveness are not verified.","observationBasis":"Source-described; full video not independently watched; post identity checked through official oEmbed","checkedAt":"2026-09-08T00:00:00Z","references":["https://newsroom.tiktok.com/cleantokawards?lang=en-GB"]},{"id":"stevie-nicks-afternoon","platform":"tiktok","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@stevienicks/video/6883220570914278662","creator":"Stevie Nicks","title":"A recognizable format survives a change of props","description":"Stevie Nicks laces roller skates with a cranberry-juice bottle in the background. Her caption names Doggface and reframes the premise as an afternoon moment.","mechanism":"Retain the audience’s recognition cues while letting each creator contribute something specific. This is variation with a reason.","limitation":"Demonstrates a credited cultural response. It cannot show that identical reposting or copying another creator’s footage would work.","observationBasis":"Source-described; full video not independently watched; post identity checked through official oEmbed","checkedAt":"2026-09-08T00:00:00Z","references":["https://newsroom.tiktok.com/doggface-gives-the-world-a-smile-with-juice-a-skateboard-and-all-the-vibes?lang=en"]}],"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T07:43:10.585Z","author":"jet","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/creative-diversity-test.jpg","width":1280,"height":676,"alt":{"en":"Colorful figures and decorative panels in a stained glass cathedral window."},"credit":"Pudelek; retouch by Albertus teolog","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: ab2b78f70b4197eba0649f9c964509668fa28271.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Vitus_Cathedral_-_Stained_glass_(retouch).jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en","next":{"id":"068","slug":"native-features-test","term":"Native features","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"native-features-test","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["zero-view-rate","creative-diversity-test","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"TikTok Native Features: Test Their Creative Contribution","dek":"A native-feature test separates a feature’s effect from its publishing channel.","point":"A native-feature test separates a feature’s effect from its publishing channel. Comparing whole workflows does not always allow that separation.","body":["If one group uses audio or formatting absent from the other, treatment no longer concerns upload method alone. Document features precisely. Depending on the question, accept that bundle of differences or design a narrower test. State honestly what the comparison measures.","A protocol may deliberately compare two complete experiences when that is the team’s actual decision. Name the treatment accordingly. The aim is not to remove all complexity but to avoid a narrow conclusion from a broad test. Keep the result’s wording at the scale of what changed. A workflow comparison can be practically useful without identifying the isolated contribution of every feature inside it."],"action":["Inventory feature differences.","Choose a feature test or a workflow test."],"trap":"A gap between workflows does not identify which component produced the effect.","quote":"Maybe it is not native. Maybe it is the feature.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Maybe it is not native. Maybe it is the feature.","text":"A native-feature test separates a feature’s effect from its publishing channel.","media":"/images/editorial/native-features-test.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Native features","text":"A native-feature test separates a feature’s effect from its publishing channel. Comparing whole workflows does not always allow that separation.","media":"/images/editorial/native-features-test.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A gap between workflows does not identify which component produced the effect.","media":"/images/editorial/native-features-test.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Inventory feature differences.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/native-features-test.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Choose a feature test or a workflow test.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/native-features-test.jpg"}]}]},"workshops":[{"id":"video","title":"Prepare the actual video slot, not just the caption","intro":"TokPortal’s editor distinguishes Video, Carousel and Story, and asks for a target publishing period. The API follows the same operational idea: the content needs a valid format, accessible media and a usable window.","endpoint":"PUT /api/ext/bundles/{id}/videos/{position}","code":"{\n  \"tool\": \"tokportal_configure_bundle_video\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"id\": \"<real-bundle-uuid>\",\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"body\": {\n      \"video_type\": \"video\",\n      \"video_url\": \"<public_url returned by your video upload>\",\n      \"description\": \"A practical example of organising freelance subscriptions.\",\n      \"target_publish_date\": \"<valid future date: YYYY-MM-DD>\"\n    }\n  }\n}","language":"json","explain":"Replace the marked values with your actual upload and bundle. This template is intentionally not a runnable campaign. target_publish_date starts a two-day publishing window; it does not request an exact minute.","checks":[{"label":"Choose the correct media fields","detail":"A video needs video_url and description. A TikTok carousel instead needs carousel_images and tiktok_sound_url."},{"label":"Use a valid window","detail":"Allow at least three days while account creation is pending, or one day for delivered/existing accounts. Check the current response and limits."},{"label":"Inspect readiness","detail":"GET /api/ext/bundles/{id}/publish-readiness lists blockers without a debit or mutation. Review ignored_fields and the returned start/end dates."}],"sources":["https://developers.tokportal.com/mcp/"],"checkedAt":"2026-09-09T00:00:00Z","capture":{"src":"/images/tokportal/tokportal-video-editor.png","width":650,"height":565,"alt":"Two real TokPortal editor views showing media format, caption and target publishing period.","caption":"Two cropped views of the real video editor, captured 8 September 2026. Historical dates shown; use a valid future window for a new task.","source":"https://app.tokportal.com/dashboard"}}],"schemaVersion":2,"deepDive":{"heading":"A feature is part of a package","paragraphs":["A post using an in-app effect, sound or interactive feature differs from a plain upload in several ways at once. The feature may alter the creative, the audience's recognition and the production process. An observed performance difference does not automatically prove that the platform rewards the publishing route. Start by describing the actual feature and the hypothesised mechanism. Does it clarify the joke, invite a useful response or make the content recognisable in a conversation people already understand? That is a more useful question than assuming a hidden bonus.","Document which features are available for the account and method at the time of testing. Platform capabilities change, and a comparison can become obsolete without the headline changing. Keep content rights and commercial-use permissions in scope, especially for music. Use comparable creative treatments and a fixed observation window, then report both the outcome and the limits of the design. A feature may be worth adopting because it improves the post or reduces operator work even when a separate distribution advantage remains unproven."],"diagram":{"kind":"compare","title":"Separate the reasons a feature helps","items":[{"label":"Creative","detail":"Does it make the idea clearer or more compelling?","value":0},{"label":"Workflow","detail":"Does it reduce a documented publishing constraint?","value":0},{"label":"Distribution","detail":"Is there evidence beyond an observed association?","value":0}],"caption":"Editorial model: a way to reason about the process, not measured platform results."},"caseLens":"Study the feature's visible contribution to the post. Do not infer a platform ranking preference from its presence alone.","caseIds":[]},"examples":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T07:41:56.167Z","author":"jet","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/native-features-test.jpg","width":1280,"height":824,"alt":{"en":"Camera lenses of different sizes and focal lengths arranged on a shelf."},"credit":"Carlos Valenzuela Montuy","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 64ce48e9dc3b2aa2cc7497d42862acec291b1373.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Photographic_lenses_and_tubes_2025.jpg","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"}},"previous":{"id":"066","slug":"formatted-vs-chaotic","term":"Formatted vs chaotic","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"formatted-vs-chaotic","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["creative-diversity-test","slideshow-vs-video","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"TikTok Content Strategy: Recurring Series vs Spontaneous Posts","dek":"A Formatted versus Chaotic test compares a recurring structure with multiple formats.","point":"A Formatted versus Chaotic test compares a recurring structure with multiple formats. It needs a shared editorial objective and documented variation.","body":["A series may improve operating consistency; a flexible account may explore more angles. Measure creative workload and concepts tested too. Otherwise you may compare a well-resourced system with an underfunded one. This protocol presumes no winner.","Archive the concepts actually published in each group. A chaotic account may appear stronger because it received the best subjects. A series may appear more stable because its variations were less ambitious. A creative record makes these differences discussable instead of hiding them behind a format label. The result should explain the tested systems, not imply that one loosely defined category has defeated another in every possible context."],"action":["Define fixed elements in each group.","Compare invested resources."],"trap":"One campaign’s outcome does not become a universal rule about formats.","quote":"Series or chaos? A test, not a taste war.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Series or chaos? A test, not a taste war.","text":"A Formatted versus Chaotic test compares a recurring structure with multiple formats.","media":"/images/editorial/formatted-vs-chaotic.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Formatted vs chaotic","text":"A Formatted versus Chaotic test compares a recurring structure with multiple formats. It needs a shared editorial objective and documented variation.","media":"/images/editorial/formatted-vs-chaotic.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"One campaign’s outcome does not become a universal rule about formats.","media":"/images/editorial/formatted-vs-chaotic.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Define fixed elements in each group.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/formatted-vs-chaotic.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Compare invested resources.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/formatted-vs-chaotic.jpg"}]}]},"workshops":[],"schemaVersion":2,"deepDive":{"heading":"The controlled variable is recognisability","paragraphs":["A repeatable format gives viewers a stable way into the idea. A deliberately looser post can feel immediate and surprising. The mistake is to compare a polished recurring series with a careless outtake and conclude that structure beats chaos, or to compare a brilliant spontaneous moment with a lifeless template and conclude the opposite. Define what changes between the treatments: opening rhythm, visual consistency, narrative order or production finish. Keep the audience problem and the quality of the underlying observation as similar as the experiment allows.","Look beyond the first spike. A recurring format can become easier to produce and recognise, but also easier to ignore when the examples stop teaching anything new. A looser style can create memorable moments while depending heavily on an individual creator's judgement. Record production effort, useful audience responses and whether the account remains coherent across several posts. The decision may be a mix: stable editorial promises with flexible execution. A format is infrastructure for an idea, not a replacement for having something worth saying."],"diagram":{"kind":"compare","title":"Structure and surprise can coexist","items":[{"label":"Promise","detail":"Keep the audience's reason to return clear.","value":0},{"label":"Execution","detail":"Vary how the observation is delivered.","value":0},{"label":"Review","detail":"Inspect recognition, fatigue and production effort.","value":0}],"caption":"Editorial model: a way to reason about the process, not measured platform results."},"caseLens":"The post offers an example of execution. A single clip cannot establish that a loose or repeatable style wins across accounts.","caseIds":[]},"examples":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T07:41:56.167Z","author":"jet","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/formatted-vs-chaotic.jpg","width":1280,"height":843,"alt":{"en":"An upward view through the sweeping spiral staircase at the Vatican Museums."},"credit":"Colin","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 26b9dc66ea2c1b295e5c1834a652b763214cad24.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vatican_Museums_Spiral_Staircase_Looking_Up_2012.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0"}}}],"$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16"]}]
