19:["$","p","1",{"children":"The sink-cleaning example makes sound part of the stated creative treatment. A useful exploration would compare genuinely different ways of explaining a relevant task, not merely swap the music while keeping every promise identical. One treatment might emphasise the transformation, another the difficult step and another the sensory process. Those are candidate hypotheses about what makes the activity interesting. Give each an original, rights-cleared execution and define the intended outcome before publishing. The presence of a named product in the reference is observable context; sponsorship and commercial effectiveness remain separate questions that the available evidence does not resolve."}]
